  Here's the thread about another poster having this same problem.

<http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_thread/thread/5b8b5f177e9ae8d1/?hide_quotes=no#msg_baa01da2a9c296dc>


  Here's the post with the solution.

<http://groups.google.com/groups?as_umsgid=1141487835.679263.89080@z34g2000cwc.googlegroups.com>

Add these lines to your NetHack configuration file (defaults.nh on
MSDOS/Windows):

SOUNDDIR=C:\Games\Nethack\Sounds
SOUND=MESG "*hungry*" "alert.wav" 50
SOUND=MESG "*needs food*" "alert.wav" 50
SOUND=MESG "*weak*" "alert.wav" 50


  Note that you'll have to create the C:\Games\Nethack\Sounds directory
on Windows.  Or create another directory if you're not on Windows.  Then
you'll have to copy the "alert.wav" file into the directory.


  For full explanation of NetHack sounds see the Section 9.8 of the
Guidebook at <http://www.nethack.org/v343/Guidebook.html>.



